    "knowledge_point": "Finding Exact Values Using the Sum and Difference Formulas",
    "problem": "Find the exact value of  $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{195}^{∘}.$\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${195}^{∘}={135}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}.$*",
    "worked_solution": "Recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for cosine with $x={135}^{∘}$ and $y={60}^{∘}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({195}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡({135}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{135}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{135}^{∘}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{6}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
